💡 **SUGGESTION picked up — zero-bullet bodies are now an `EntryProblem` (commit `1eb9f7b5fa`)**

`scripts/gen_changelog.dart` (`_parseEntry`), right at the existing bullet count:

```dart
final bullets = body.split('\n').where((l) => l.startsWith('- ')).length;
if (bullets == 0) {
  problems.add(
    EntryProblem(name, 'body must be 1–3 `- ` bullet lines — prose without '
        'bullets breaks the flat release-notes shape'),
  );
  return null;
}
if (bullets > 3) { … ::warning:: … }   // unchanged — warn-and-pass
```

Both directions pinned in the `--validate` test group of `test/changelog_gen_test.dart`:

- **0 bullets → red** (new): `bullet-less prose body fails (notes shape is 1–3 `- ` lines)` — a prose body (`Just a prose paragraph with no bullet lines at all.`) now exits 1 with `::error::` naming the file and the message. RED-first verified: exit 0 on the pre-fix branch.
- **4 bullets → warn** (already pinned, unchanged): `more than 3 bullets warns but passes` asserts exit 0 + `::warning::`.

The flat-bullets aggregate shape the AC2 parity test pins can no longer be silently diverged from by a prose-only entry.
